Package: nextgenCrossWorkbench
Type: Package
Title: A Shiny Interface for Genomic Cross Prediction and Mate Allocation
Version: 0.10.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mario", "Morales", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "mario.morales.44@gmail.com"),
    person("Sikiru", "Atanda", role = "aut",
           comment = "Author of the 'nextgenCrossDesign' backend engine"),
    person("North Dakota State University", role = "cph"))
Description: A point-and-click 'shiny' front-end for genomic cross prediction
    and mate allocation in plant and animal breeding programs. It guides the
    user through genomic prediction of cross performance (progeny mean,
    variance and the usefulness criterion), multi-trait objectives, and
    optimum-contribution-style mate allocation that balances genetic gain
    against diversity, over plain 'CSV' inputs. Additional features include an
    automatic cross-number optimizer, robust (posterior) allocation, a
    dosage-aware polyploid design workflow, and a self-contained interactive
    'HTML' report. The breeding-genetics computations are performed by the
    companion 'nextgenCrossDesign' engine, which is driven as a separate,
    user-configured R process (see 'SystemRequirements'); the front-end itself
    installs and runs independently. Methods build on the usefulness criterion
    of Lehermeier, Teyssedre and Schoen (2017) <doi:10.1534/genetics.117.300403>
    and genomic mating of Akdemir and Sanchez (2016)
    <doi:10.3389/fgene.2016.00210>.
